{"status":"ok","data":{"mode":"Local structured explainer","label":"Structured explainer — deterministic text from engine outputs (not AI-generated)","question":"Why did profit attributable to our shareholders change between V1 and V2?","answer":"Profit attributable to owners of the parent rose by €2 (€1,685 in V1 → €1,687 in V2); group profit moved (€2,210 → €2,225) and closing cash was flat (€25,630 → €25,630).\n\nSource: RVS corrected intercompany invoice RVS-INV to RVL from €2,000 to €2,100, and RVL corrected its reciprocal invoice RVL-PINV to match. The intercompany sale is eliminated in full, so group revenue does not move.\n\nWhat moved is the margin RVS earned on goods still held in RVL's inventory. ELIM_UNREALISED_MARGIN removed €250 in V1 (journal RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V1:ELIM_UNREALISED_MARGIN@v1:RVS>RVL) and €300 in V2 (journal RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V2-2:ELIM_UNREALISED_MARGIN@v1:RVS>RVL). Deferred tax on that margin at RVL's tax rate (ELIM_UPM_DEFERRED_TAX) is €75 in V1 (journal RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V1:ELIM_UPM_DEFERRED_TAX@v1:RVS>RVL) and €90 in V2 (journal RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V2-2:ELIM_UPM_DEFERRED_TAX@v1:RVS>RVL); it is the only part of the change that reaches group profit.\n\nRVS is the seller (upstream), so non-controlling interests bear their share: NCI = 40% × (850 − 0) = 340 in V1 (journal RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V1:ATTRIB_NCI@v1:RVA) vs 40% × (850 − 0) = 340 in V2 (journal RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V2-2:ATTRIB_NCI@v1:RVA).\n\nProfit to owners of the parent = group profit − NCI share: 2,210 − 340 = 1,685 vs 2,225 − 340 = 1,687.","amounts":[{"token":"€2","value":"2.00","source":{"runId":"RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V2-2","kind":"compare","key":"compare.attr.parent","field":"absDelta"}},{"token":"€1,685","value":"1685.00","source":{"runId":"RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V1","kind":"statement","key":"attr.parent","field":"amount"}},{"token":"€1,687","value":"1687.00","source":{"runId":"RUN-RVGDED3-20261122124658-V2-2","kind":